notes: "HUANDENG is built on open work, but the relationships differ. OpenSlide is the editor code foundation under MIT. OpenPPTD contributes only the MathML-to-OMML formula conversion modules, not the whole document model. PptxGenJS generates the PPTX export; Apache ECharts, KaTeX and Font Awesome are dependencies for charts, formulas and icons. PowerPoint and WPS are the file-and-canvas model this project reacts to. Kimi/Moonshot and open-kimi-ppt-skill are where I first met the PPTD approach; this is not a claim that Kimi invented a standard. PPTist, Slidev, Presenton, PPTAgent, PPTMaster, OpenSlides Studio (openslides.dev), OPF and VS Code are workflow inspiration and researched alternatives. HUANDENG is not affiliated with or endorsed by Kimi or the named projects. The not-yet list keeps the talk from implying completeness.\n\nReference URLs (names link to source repositories or official sites):\nHUANDENG: https://github.com/JaytonKogeru/huandeng\nOpenSlide: https://github.com/open-slide/open-slide\nOpenPPTD: https://github.com/Shingwha/open-pptd\nPptxGenJS: https://github.com/gitbrent/PptxGenJS\nPowerPoint: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/powerpoint\nWPS: https://www.wps.com/\nKimi / Moonshot AI: https://www.kimi.com/\nopen-kimi-ppt-skill: https://github.com/Amonginin/open-kimi-ppt-skill\nPPTist: https://github.com/pipipi-pikachu/PPTist\nVS Code: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode\nSlidev: https://github.com/slidevjs/slidev\nPresenton: https://github.com/presenton/presenton\nPPTAgent: https://github.com/icip-cas/PPTAgent\nPPTMaster: https://github.com/hugohe3/ppt-master\nOpenSlides Studio: https://gitlab.com/open-slides/openslides\nOPF: https://github.com/OpenPresentation/opf\nApache ECharts: https://github.com/apache/echarts\nKaTeX: https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX\nFont Awesome: https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome\nOpenSlides Studio website: https://openslides.dev/\nOPF website: https://www.openpresentation.org/\n"
